        "message": "Add self-service password recovery with single-use reset tokens\n\nA forgotten password used to mean an admin reading a temporary password\naloud. Now the sign-in page links to a recovery form: the request endpoint\nalways answers the same 202 so it cannot be used to discover who is\nregistered, and a real account gets a 32-byte token whose SHA-256 hash is\nthe only thing stored (V9).\n\nA link expires after 30 minutes and works once, enforced by claiming the\nrow with a conditional update, so a double submit cannot both succeed.\nRequesting a new link kills the old one, and redeeming a token bumps the\naccount's token version to sign out any session opened before the reset.\n\nMail is optional: with MAIL_HOST blank the link is logged at WARN, which\nkeeps the demo usable without SMTP. Setting the MAIL_* variables and\nAPP_BASE_URL turns it into real email.",
        "timestamp": "2026-11-13T12:30:48Z",
