        "message": "Refuse an import that has nothing to import\n\nDropping the empty-roster overloads exposed why they were dangerous: called from\nthe class itself they skip the transactional proxy, so the annotation on the real\nmethod was never applied. They are gone, and the real one now carries it.\n\nThe same pass found the import answering 200 to a list of blanks and accepting a\nwhole year group in one request. Both are now 400s, with a 500-address cap.",
